"MODEL_RESPONSE_OBTAINED"}},{"stepId":"gate-corrected","capabilityId":"sql-database-reader","historicalBasis":"probe 2f19a147: ran (CENSUS_READY, 69 of 69 fulfilled); format-labels round one 61408844 (67 of 69)","input":{"dataSource":"sfx-estate-database","statement":"EXEC analysis.check_census_fulfillment @input=@input;","resultColumn":"value","input":{"censusText":"(bound)","obligationsText":"(bound)","judgmentText":"(bound)","idStatus":"(bound)","idFeedback":"(bound)"}},"bind":[{"target":"input.censusText","fromStep":"check-corrected","path":"$.value.censusJson"},{"target":"input.obligationsText","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.obligations"},{"target":"input.judgmentText","fromStep":"judge-corrected","path":"$.response.text"},{"target":"input.idStatus","fromStep":"check-corrected","path":"$.value.status"},{"target":"input.idFeedback","fromStep":"check-corrected","path":"$.value.feedback"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.value.ran","equals":1}},{"stepId":"correct-again","capabilityId":"ask-model","historicalBasis":"probe 5f6b8116: MODEL_RESPONSE_OBTAINED, a patch replacing 1 area; format-labels round two 0e748ee8","input":{"requestId":"ov3-harness-census-correct","modelRequest":{"interaction":{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You decompose the product a specification describes into capability areas for the SideFX estate, where every capability is declared data and holds exactly one canonical feature. The product is OV3 itself: the agentic harness that takes an objective and owns the work - assembling evidence, planning, coordinating specialists, executing, checking results against the owner''s intent, correcting gaps, and building and improving itself. The recorded projects are evidence of what the harness must do and of the work it has run; a project''s own domain (for example financial analysis, resume documents or infrastructure) is not a harness area, but the harness need that the project reveals is. The first user message is the specification. The second lists the installed capability ids. The third is a JSON array of the recorded obligations, each with an id and its text: every tracker project, every task of the project, and every owner direction. Aim for at most 30 areas; the census must never exceed 60. Each area is one capability the harness needs, named by a proposed capability id (lowercase ASCII letters, digits, dots and hyphens; unique), with its name (a few words), its responsibility (what it does and what it guarantees, at most 300 characters), covers (which of elaborate-planning, self-improvement, multi-agent-consensus, control-plane, deterministic-multi-step-execution and other the area serves), answers (the ids of the obligations from the third message this area is responsible for; at least one), and existingCapabilities (installed capability ids from the second message that the area extends or reuses; empty when none or when unsure). Every obligation in the third message must be answered by at least one area. Each of elaborate-planning, self-improvement, multi-agent-consensus, control-plane and deterministic-multi-step-execution must be covered by at least one area. Use only the given material. Cite only ids that appear verbatim in the second and third messages; never invent an obligation or capability id. The fourth user message is the current census and the fifth lists its defects, found by two checks against the obligations: a deterministic check that every obligation id is answered, and a separate fulfillment check that judged whether each area''s name and responsibility actually do what each obligation it claims requires. Return one JSON object with only the changes that fix every listed defect: areas, each a complete area that replaces the area with the same capabilityId or is added, and remove, the capabilityIds of areas to delete. Areas you do not list stay as they are. Every unfulfilled obligation must end up answered by an area whose responsibility does what it requires: extend a fitting area''s responsibility and answers, or add an area. A rejected claim must not remain: replace the area without it, or rewrite the area so that it fulfills it. A project whose own domain is not a harness area (for example resume documents, financial analysis, infrastructure or publishing) is answered by the harness area that provides what its work needs, such as declaring, building and running domain capabilities from a specification, never by an area that does the domain work itself. When the census would exceed 60 areas, merge: remove areas and replace another so that its responsibility and answers cover theirs. If the fifth message says No defects., return empty areas and remove."},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"}]},"responsePolicy":{"format":"json","schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["areas","remove"],"properties":{"areas":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["capabilityId","name","responsibility","covers","answers","existingCapabilities"],"properties":{"capabilityId":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*$"},"name":{"type":"string"},"responsibility":{"type":"string","maxLength":300},"covers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["elaborate-planning","self-improvement","multi-agent-consensus","control-plane","deterministic-multi-step-execution","other"]}},"answers":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"string"}},"existingCapabilities":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},"remove":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}},"maximumOutputTokens":12000,"temperature":0.2}}},"bind":[{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[1].content","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.text"},{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[2].content","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.capabilityIds"},{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[3].content","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.obligations"},{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[4].content","fromStep":"check-corrected","path":"$.value.censusJson"},{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[5].content","fromStep":"gate-corrected","path":"$.value.feedback"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.disposition","equals":"MODEL_RESPONSE_OBTAINED"}},{"stepId":"apply-again","capabilityId":"sql-database-reader","historicalBasis":"probe 76fce241: patchIsJson 1","input":{"dataSource":"sfx-estate-database","statement":"EXEC analysis.apply_census_patch @input=@input;","resultColumn":"value","input":{"censusText":"(bound)","patchText":"(bound)"}},"bind":[{"target":"input.censusText","fromStep":"check-corrected","path":"$.value.censusJson"},{"target":"input.patchText","fromStep":"correct-again","path":"$.response.text"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.value.patchIsJson","equals":1}},{"stepId":"check-again","capabilityId":"sql-database-reader","historicalBasis":"probe b81d7432: ran (CENSUS_READY)","input":{"dataSource":"sfx-estate-database","statement":"EXEC analysis.check_capability_census @input=@input;","resultColumn":"value","input":{"censusText":"(bound)","obligationsText":"(bound)","requiredCoverage":"elaborate-planning,self-improvement,multi-agent-consensus,control-plane,deterministic-multi-step-execution","specDigest":"sha256:a344104861ea0cb7e9557cc9b359a9e9567f7f3e921477d0cd596de0a6413c09","maxAreas":60}},"bind":[{"target":"input.censusText","fromStep":"apply-again","path":"$.value.census"},{"target":"input.obligationsText","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.obligations"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.value.ran","equals":1}},{"stepId":"judge-again","capabilityId":"ask-model","historicalBasis":"probe dbd7405b: MODEL_RESPONSE_OBTAINED, 69 verdicts","input":{"requestId":"ov3-harness-census-judge","modelRequest":{"interaction":{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You check a capability-area census of OV3, the agentic harness that takes an objective and owns the work: assembling evidence, planning, coordinating specialists, executing, checking results against the owner''s intent, correcting gaps, and building and improving itself. The first user message is a JSON array of the recorded obligations, each with an id and its text. The second is the census: its areas, each with a capabilityId, a name, a responsibility, and answers (the obligation ids the area claims). For every obligation, decide which of the areas that claim it fulfill it. An area fulfills an obligation only when its name and responsibility, read literally, describe work that does what the obligation requires. Claiming the id is not enough, and neither is a covers label, a generic responsibility or a shared topic word. A tracker project obligation names work the harness ran or must run; an area fulfills it when its responsibility provides the harness capability that work needs, for example declaring, building and running the project''s domain capabilities from its specification. An area that does a project''s domain work itself, for example writing resume documents, analysing financial markets or provisioning infrastructure, is not a harness area and fulfills nothing. Return one JSON object with verdicts: one per obligation in the first message, in its order, each with obligationId, fulfilledBy (the capabilityIds of claiming areas that fulfill it; empty when none does) and reason (one short sentence: what the fulfilling area does that meets the obligation, or why no claiming area does). Never name an area that does not claim the obligation."},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"},{"role":"user","content":"(bound)"}]},"responsePolicy":{"format":"json","schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["verdicts"],"properties":{"verdicts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["obligationId","fulfilledBy","reason"],"properties":{"obligationId":{"type":"string"},"fulfilledBy":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"reason":{"type":"string","maxLength":200}}}}}},"maximumOutputTokens":12000,"temperature":0}}},"bind":[{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[1].content","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.obligations"},{"target":"modelRequest.interaction.messages[2].content","fromStep":"check-again","path":"$.value.censusJson"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.disposition","equals":"MODEL_RESPONSE_OBTAINED"}},{"stepId":"gate-again","capabilityId":"sql-database-reader","historicalBasis":"probe d559249b: ran (CENSUS_READY); format-labels round two 92d35a18 (CENSUS_READY, 69 of 69)","input":{"dataSource":"sfx-estate-database","statement":"EXEC analysis.check_census_fulfillment @input=@input;","resultColumn":"value","input":{"censusText":"(bound)","obligationsText":"(bound)","judgmentText":"(bound)","idStatus":"(bound)","idFeedback":"(bound)"}},"bind":[{"target":"input.censusText","fromStep":"check-again","path":"$.value.censusJson"},{"target":"input.obligationsText","fromStep":"read-sources","path":"$.value.obligations"},{"target":"input.judgmentText","fromStep":"judge-again","path":"$.response.text"},{"target":"input.idStatus","fromStep":"check-again","path":"$.value.status"},{"target":"input.idFeedback","fromStep":"check-again","path":"$.value.feedback"}],"obligationIds":["O4"],"expect":{"path":"$.value.ran","equals":1}},{"stepId":"select-census","capabilityId":"sql-database-reader","historicalBasis":"probe 636b186c: CENSUS_READY, round 1 kept; format-labels 23d8c2d7: CENSUS_READY, round 2 kept; self-test 13ad6f23","input":{"dataSource":"sfx-estate-database","statement":"EXEC analysis.select_census_result @input=@input;","resultColumn":"value","input":{"firstStatus":"(bound)","firstCensus":"(bound)","firstMarkdown":"(bound)","firstFeedback":"(bound)","secondStatus":"(bound)","secondCensus":"(bound)","secondMarkdown":"(bound)","s